## End-to-end usage

- Follow the steps above to customize ESLint rules for TypeScript in your project.
- When explaining changes to teammates, point to the example sections in this README to illustrate how to comment code blocks effectively.

### Quick reference
- Inline comment: // This is an inline comment
- Block comment: /* This is a block comment */

### Notes
- Remember to keep comments concise and focused on intent rather than restating the obvious.
- Avoid over-commenting; prefer self-explanatory variable and function names plus concise commentary where necessary.

### Versioning and compatibility
- This README uses common JS/TS syntax blocks to illustrate ESLint configuration and TypeScript usage inside a Vite + React setup.

### Troubleshooting
- If comments cause syntax highlighting issues in previews, ensure code blocks are properly closed and the language specifier matches the code language.

